# JAX runtime discipline

Use:

- `jax.numpy` as `jnp`
- explicit PRNG keys
- pure numerical kernels
- `lax.scan` for time loops
- `vmap` for batches/seeds/candidates
- `jit` only hot numerical paths

Avoid:

- Python object mutation inside `jit`
- file I/O inside `jit`
- plotting inside `jit`
- JSON/markdown generation inside `jit`
- global PRNG state
- accidental float64 unless explicitly requested

When timing JAX:

- warm up separately
- call `block_until_ready` before stopping timers
- report what phases are timed and excluded

For publication benchmarks:

- local environment receipt only
- no speedup claims unless benchmark design supports them
